From fe6693c5a6134a647b6be89f7a66971039609c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude [team]" <claude-team@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strata-glm G4 stage 1: layer-pipeline stages (--layer-split
 K1,K2,.. --gpus D0,D1,..)

Each stage is an Engine for layers [lo, hi) on its own GPU: it loads only its layers (the first the
embedding, the last the head), ranks and holds only its own experts in VRAM/RAM (rebalance and RAM
admission never pull another stage's pair), splits the RAM budget instead of the first stage taking
it all, and does not predict/prefetch across its last layer. The driver moves the mHC streams
(4 x 4096 fp32 a token) between stages with cudaMemcpyPeer. One stage (the default) is the original
engine. Not run yet: needs a GPU (bit-exact check: --layer-split 14,25,35 with every stage on GPU 0).
---
 src/glm/glm_main.cpp | 271 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 185 insertions(+), 86 deletions(-)

